WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.501
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:16.296
Unit fifteen: Conditional Variations. Today you will use unless, provided that, as long as and in case.

4
00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:19.516
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.758
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:25.664
Unless.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.232
Unless means if not.

8
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:30.839
Unless you hurry, you'll be late.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.021
Your turn. Say: Unless.

10
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:37.984
Unless.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.856
Provided that.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.571
Provided that means only if.

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:45.450
Provided that you pay, you may enter.

14
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.062
Your turn. Say: Provided that.

15
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.133
Provided that.

16
00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:55.024
As long as.

17
00:00:56.017 --> 00:00:57.714
As long as means only if.

18
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.898
I'll go as long as you come.

19
00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:03.426
Your turn. Say: As long as.

20
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.558
As long as.

21
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:09.295
In case.

22
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:12.283
In case means as a precaution.

23
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.034
Take an umbrella in case it rains.

24
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.349
Your turn. Say: In case.

25
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.259
In case.

26
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:24.610
Alternative conditional.

27
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:29.462
Alternative conditional means a different way of expressing a condition.

28
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.864
An alternative conditional.

29
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.660
Your turn. Say: Alternative conditional.

30
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.128
Alternative conditional.

31
00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:41.850
Condition.

32
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.685
Condition means something that must happen first.

33
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:47.621
A clear condition.

34
00:01:48.217 --> 00:01:50.706
Your turn. Say: Condition.

35
00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:54.498
Condition.

36
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.298
Restriction.

37
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.900
Restriction means a limit.

38
00:01:59.483 --> 00:02:01.100
A restriction applies.

39
00:02:01.683 --> 00:02:04.475
Your turn. Say: Restriction.

40
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:08.578
Restriction.

41
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:10.260
Requirement.

42
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.726
Requirement means something necessary.

43
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.457
A requirement.

44
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.818
Your turn. Say: Requirement.

45
00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:22.621
Requirement.

46
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:26.968
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.817 --> 00:02:29.897
Visal, which word means 'if not'?

48
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:43.098
Unless means if not: Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus. We use a positive verb after unless, never a negative: not unless you don't hurry.

49
00:02:44.183 --> 00:02:46.322
What about provided that and as long as?

50
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:59.383
They both mean only if: You can borrow my car provided that you drive carefully. I'll help as long as you try. They add a restriction or requirement to the condition.

51
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:01.682
And in case?

52
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:14.471
In case is not a real conditional. It means as a precaution: Take an umbrella in case it rains. Compare: Take an umbrella if it rains means use it only then.

53
00:03:15.633 --> 00:03:17.099
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.909
Grammar focus: Conditional alternatives: unless, provided that, as long as, in case.

55
00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:25.268
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.983 --> 00:03:28.645
Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.

57
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.269
You can borrow it, provided that you drive carefully.

58
00:03:33.183 --> 00:03:35.345
Take an umbrella in case it rains.

59
00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:45.262
Unless = if not. Provided that / as long as = only if. In case = as a precaution. Use present tense in the condition clause.

60
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:50.202
Be careful! Don't say: Unless you don't hurry, you'll be late.

61
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.677
Say: Unless you hurry, you'll be late.

62
00:03:54.977 --> 00:03:57.383
Use a positive verb after unless.

63
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.819
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.633 --> 00:04:03.087
Other Conditions.

65
00:04:03.387 --> 00:04:06.246
Unless you hurry, you will miss the last bus.

66
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:10.197
You can borrow my car provided that you drive carefully.

67
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.629
I will help you as long as you try your best.

68
00:04:14.633 --> 00:04:16.993
Take an umbrella in case it rains later.

69
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.487
Each of these is a condition or a restriction.

70
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.252
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:27.117 --> 00:04:29.174
blank you study, you won't pass.

72
00:04:29.474 --> 00:04:33.116
A, Unless. B, Provided. C, In case.

73
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.446
The answer is A: Unless.

74
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:41.815
You can go blank you come back by ten.

75
00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:46.395
A, unless. B, as long as. C, in case.

76
00:04:49.933 --> 00:04:51.910
The answer is B: as long as.

77
00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.003
Take a jacket blank it gets cold.

78
00:04:55.303 --> 00:04:58.910
A, unless. B, in case. C, if not.

79
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:04.478
The answer is B: in case.

80
00:05:05.617 --> 00:05:07.105
'Unless' means blank.

81
00:05:07.405 --> 00:05:11.024
A, if not. B, only if. C, because.

82
00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:16.613
The answer is A: if not.

83
00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.574
According to the reading, what should you take?

84
00:05:20.874 --> 00:05:24.957
A, an umbrella. B, a bag. C, a map.

85
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.650
The answer is A: an umbrella.

86
00:05:31.867 --> 00:05:35.320
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:36.183 --> 00:05:39.506
Write a sentence using 'unless' and a sentence using 'as long as'.

88
00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:49.887
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.187 --> 00:06:02.803
Unless I finish my homework, I can't go out. I can go to the party as long as I am home before ten. Unless means if not, and as long as means only if.

90
00:06:03.103 --> 00:06:04.882
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:12.824
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conditional alternatives: unless, provided that, as long as, in case.

92
00:06:13.124 --> 00:06:17.565
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

93
00:06:17.865 --> 00:06:20.645
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:20.945 --> 00:06:24.665
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

